`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed acceptance contract."})," Before transformation, record units/basis, extension inventory, external resource identities, scene hierarchy, material slots and animation/skin expectations. Retain the complete validator report and tool version for both original and candidate. Treat unsupported required extensions and missing external resources as explicit blockers. Then compare the candidate's geometry, scene identities and sampled deformation in the actual consuming importer. A structurally valid asset can still lose intended material behavior, animation or collision semantics."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Failure/recovery/persistence."})," Preserve originals and transform settings. An importer returning an object is not proof that every authored feature survived. Retry corrected candidates in new output locations; never overwrite the only source or infer atomic export/rollback from a successful function return. Fresh-process reopen plus an external-resource inventory is an additional proposed gate."]}),`
