`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Ordinary SuperSplat export composes a -180° Z rotation (described in code as undoing the load-time convention), the entity world matrix, and the per-instance transform palette. It transforms positions, rotations and scales, rotates retained SH coefficients, and bakes color/transparency grading. The internal ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"keepWorldTransform=true"})," option skips the world/PLY-flip part; it does not suppress palette transforms. These facts are a source-specific convention, not a universal axis-conversion recipe."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The export source explicitly declares one LOD, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"model: 'default'"}),", and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"extraColumns: []"}),". Its comment says the editing pipeline does not carry antialiased/2DGS trained-model tags through loading. SH output is capped by the chosen maximum and available data. Therefore an uncompressed export is not proof of preservation of original metadata, LOD structure, arbitrary custom columns or all SH bands."]}),`
