`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["For a glTF pipeline, the proposed check is ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ktx validate --gltf-basisu --warnings-as-errors --format json asset.ktx2"}),". This is a documented command proposal, not an executed result. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--gltf-basisu"})," enables the extension-specific checks; ordinary KTX validation is not the same policy. Warnings are not errors unless requested. When validation reaches report generation, stdout includes ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"valid"})," and a ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"messages"})," array, with issue IDs, types, messages and details. Preserve stdout and stderr separately, together with version and exit status. Argument, input-opening and early fatal errors need not produce JSON; missing or malformed JSON is a tool/report failure, not an automatic asset verdict."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The documented exit categories are 0 success, 1 argument failure, 2 I/O failure, 3 invalid input, 4 runtime/library failure, 5 unsupported operation/state, and 6 unimplemented feature. Validation failure throws the invalid-input category. Distinguish asset rejection from infrastructure/tool failures instead of labeling every nonzero exit “bad texture.”"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Pinned sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/KhronosGroup/KTX-Software/blob/4d6fc70eaf62ad0558e63e8d97eb9766118327a6/tools/ktx/command_validate.cpp",children:"validator"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/KhronosGroup/KTX-Software/blob/4d6fc70eaf62ad0558e63e8d97eb9766118327a6/tools/ktx/command.h",children:"exit codes and report formats"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"normal-mode-changes-the-shader-contract",children:"Normal-mode changes the shader contract"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--normal-mode"})," accepts linear textures with at least two components. Three/four-channel input is treated as XYZ unit normals; the fourth channel is discarded, and XY is repacked as RGB=X, A=Y. The documented reconstruction samples GA and rebuilds positive Z. This is a channel-layout transformation, not just a quality preset. Reject the preset unless the consuming shader explicitly implements that layout; retain a material-slot/encoding/channel-layout record."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--normalize"})," on a two-component input normalizes a 2D vector; its documentation explicitly warns against using that result to generate XY normals with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--normal-mode"}),". Separately, assignment of a transfer function and conversion of pixel values are different operations. Prefer explicit intent and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--fail-on-color-conversions"})," when unexpected conversion must fail the build."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Pinned sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/KhronosGroup/KTX-Software/blob/4d6fc70eaf62ad0558e63e8d97eb9766118327a6/tools/ktx/encode_utils_common.h",children:"normal-mode contract"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/KhronosGroup/KTX-Software/blob/4d6fc70eaf62ad0558e63e8d97eb9766118327a6/tools/ktx/command_create.cpp",children:"normalization and transfer-function options"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"transcodable-container-is-a-separate-gate",children:"Transcodable container is a separate gate"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The pinned transcode command requires BasisLZ or a UASTC DFD color model. It explicitly rejects an input that does not need transcoding as invalid input. Merely having a valid ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:".ktx2"})," container is insufficient. Without an explicit target, the command chooses uncompressed r8/rg8/rgb8/rgba8 based on channel count. Record the requested target and inspect output format; successful conversion alone does not prove the intended compressed GPU representation was produced."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Pinned source: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/KhronosGroup/KTX-Software/blob/4d6fc70eaf62ad0558e63e8d97eb9766118327a6/tools/ktx/command_transcode.cpp",children:"transcode implementation and help"}),". Its embedded raw-only wording conflicts with the implementation's KTX2 writer; do not repeat that wording as an established restriction without a focused upstream clarification/test."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"gltf-usage-and-payload-requirements",children:"glTF usage and payload requirements"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The official extension adds concrete gates: identity/absent swizzle, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"rd"}),"/absent orientation, 2D material images, base dimensions divisible by four, and usage-specific DFD metadata. Non-color data requires unspecified primaries plus linear transfer; color data requires BT.709 primaries plus sRGB. Premultiplied-alpha flag is forbidden unless the material specification requires it. Full mips are SHOULD, not MUST, for mipmapped or unspecified samplers. For non-color UASTC without ASTC/BC7, the specification recommends uncompressed RGBA to avoid artifacts."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Source: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF/blob/521a91d491f02bb7db7d445b35f591d09d2a64ce/extensions/2.0/Khronos/KHR_texture_basisu/README.md",children:"KHR_texture_basisu"}),". Source revision: 521a91d491f02bb7db7d445b35f591d09d2a64ce. The extension classifies standard normal maps as RGB textures; Use a generic XY-in-GA preset for a standard glTF normal slot only with an explicit compatible shader/encoding contract. No reviewed source established an alpha-coverage-preserving mip guarantee; do not equate a full pyramid or successful validation with preserved cutout coverage."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed evidence and recovery:"})," retain source texture/material role, all invocation arguments, tool pin, validation policy/report/exit status, input/output hashes, channel mapping, transfer metadata, dimensions/mip inventory and requested/actual transcode target. Quarantine incomplete candidates and retain the original. Unimplemented negative fixtures include an invalid glTF swizzle/orientation, non-transcodable valid KTX2, a two-component normalization mismatch, an early I/O failure without JSON, and a successful default transcode whose uncompressed output violates the project budget. Target GPU support, alpha-cutout coverage, codec quality and material appearance still require consumer-side tests. Neither these commands nor those fixtures were executed. Exact dependency/input-asset licensing and conversion atomicity are not established by this source review."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"4-optimize-retopologize-unwrap-and-regenerate-tangents-without-losing-correspondence",children:"4. Optimize, retopologize, unwrap and regenerate tangents without losing correspondence"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Documented operations and fields."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/blob/f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92/README.md",children:"meshoptimizer at f0a684f1"})," provides GPU-oriented optimization, simplification and compression, with gltfpack and a JavaScript subset. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/google/draco/blob/d429de84b52a860705507da0884764c5d8321423/README.md",children:"Draco at d429de84"})," compresses meshes/point clouds and provides JavaScript/WebAssembly decoders; its documentation recommends version-specific decoder URLs. These operations do not themselves establish a target importer's extension/decoder compatibility."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["At the inspected meshoptimizer snapshot, ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/blob/f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92/README.md#L548-L571",children:"basic simplification error"})," is approximate and relative to mesh extents; topology/error limits can stop reduction before the requested index count. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/blob/f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92/src/meshoptimizer.h#L466-L474",children:"SimplifyErrorAbsolute"})," changes input and reported error to absolute units; otherwise ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/blob/f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92/src/meshoptimizer.h#L609-L615",children:"simplifyScale"})," converts error units. Proposed gate: retain source units, error mode, requested/actual index counts and returned error separately from rendered or deformation fidelity."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/blob/f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92/README.md#L401-L417",children:"vertex codec"})," is lossless, while preceding quantization and ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/blob/f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92/README.md#L518-L540",children:"vertex filters"})," can lose information. Its documented default vertex/index bitstream versions are both 1, compatible with v0.23+/v0.14+ respectively; those compatibility guarantees concern point releases and exclude development branches. Record bitstream version as well as encoder/decoder identity. Draco's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/google/draco/blob/d429de84b52a860705507da0884764c5d8321423/README.md#L307-L320",children:"documented encoder CLI"})," defaults position quantization to 11 bits; zero disables quantization only for the specified attribute. Its ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/google/draco/blob/d429de84b52a860705507da0884764c5d8321423/README.md#L10-L20",children:"versioned decoder-URL guidance"})," addresses propagation/cache mismatches. Proposed gate: retain per-attribute quantization/filter settings and compare the final decoded candidate with the original; a codec label is not pipeline-wide fidelity evidence. No encoding, decoding or simplification was executed for this review."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/jpcy/xatlas/blob/f700c7790aaa030e794b52ba7791a05c085faf0c/README.md",children:"xatlas at f700c779"})," separates charting and packing. UV seams can increase output vertex count; a progress callback returning false requests cancellation. Its ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/jpcy/xatlas/blob/f700c7790aaa030e794b52ba7791a05c085faf0c/source/xatlas/xatlas.h#L58-L118",children:"output header"})," defines Vertex.xref as the output-to-input vertex mapping and uv in atlas-dimension units, not normalized coordinates. Ignored faces remain with UV (0,0) and atlasIndex -1, so nonempty output does not establish complete usable atlas coverage. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mmikk/MikkTSpace/blob/3e895b49d05ea07e4c2133156cfa94369e19e409/mikktspace.h#L79-L139",children:"MikkTSpace's pinned header"})," returns tangents per face-vertex and warns against averaging or overwriting through the old index list. Baker/renderer triangulation must match. Its ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mmikk/MikkTSpace/blob/3e895b49d05ea07e4c2133156cfa94369e19e409/mikktspace.c#L374-L419",children:"implementation"})," skips non-triangle/non-quad faces and conditionally invokes output callbacks; a true return alone does not prove every input face received stored tangents. These are source observations, not reproduced failures. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/UVAtlas",children:"UVAtlas"})," exposes create/partition/pack and remapping APIs, but was archived April 24, 2026; upstream discourages use for new projects."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/wjakob/instant-meshes",children:"Instant Meshes"})," documents orientation-field then position-field solving with interactive guidance. That workflow is not evidence of a headless automation API. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/hjwdzh/QuadriFlow",children:"QuadriFlow"})," processes OBJ geometry; its documented solver selection changes dependency licensing. Neither remesher establishes preserved skinning or animation-ready edge flow."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed acceptance contract."})," Freeze source topology and attribute ownership → create an optimization/retopology candidate → establish explicit old/new correspondence where available → unwrap and apply vertex remaps to all affected attributes → regenerate compatible tangents → bake/decode/import → compare geometry, UV seams, normal response and sampled deformation. Record decoder, triangulation and target extension support. Same index count is not proof of unchanged vertex identity."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Failure/recovery/persistence."})," Lost weight/morph correspondence, UV overlap, changed tangent signs, unsupported decoder or excessive geometric error blocks promotion. Restart from the preserved preceding stage after correcting parameters; do not repair by guessing old indices. In the pinned xatlas ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/jpcy/xatlas/blob/f700c7790aaa030e794b52ba7791a05c085faf0c/source/xatlas/xatlas.cpp#L9574-L9603",children:"repack path"}),", prior output is destroyed before cancellable packing. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/jpcy/xatlas/blob/f700c7790aaa030e794b52ba7791a05c085faf0c/source/xatlas/xatlas.cpp#L9627-L9643",children:"output array and meshCount"})," are initialized before the per-mesh loop; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/jpcy/xatlas/blob/f700c7790aaa030e794b52ba7791a05c085faf0c/source/xatlas/xatlas.cpp#L9793-L9802",children:"cancellation between mesh outputs"})," can leave later entries unbuilt. Do not infer complete output from meshCount or assume every cancellation has the same partial state. Preserve the preceding artifact separately and validate per-mesh/face coverage. These static paths were not executed. Archive only validated stage outputs as reusable inputs; generic interruption/retry guarantees remain unknown."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Unimplemented fixture:"})," mirrored UVs, a seam requiring duplicated vertices, an asymmetric quad with fixed triangulation, a skin-weight boundary and a known silhouette. Evaluate under motion and lighting; compression ratio and quad count are not quality scores."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Version/license scope:"})," xatlas is pinned to f700c7790aaa030e794b52ba7791a05c085faf0c (2022-07-25), MikkTSpace to 3e895b49d05ea07e4c2133156cfa94369e19e409 (2020-03-25; header Version 1.0), source-checked 2026-10-19. These are source snapshots, not installed versions. meshoptimizer is pinned to f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92 (header 1.3) and Draco to d429de84b52a860705507da0884764c5d8321423 (header 1.5.9), also checked 2026-10-19; neither snapshot is asserted to be a verified release tag. Other references in this section are rolling. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/blob/f0a684f11ead064e176775c9b796f82a55910e92/LICENSE.md",children:"meshoptimizer"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/jpcy/xatlas/blob/f700c7790aaa030e794b52ba7791a05c085faf0c/LICENSE",children:"xatlas"})," and UVAtlas declare MIT; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/google/draco/blob/d429de84b52a860705507da0884764c5d8321423/LICENSE",children:"Draco Apache-2.0"}),". MikkTSpace's permissive notice has origin, altered-source and notice-preservation conditions. Instant Meshes has a ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wjakob/instant-meshes/master/LICENSE.txt",children:"license with supplemental terms"}),", requiring full review. QuadriFlow is MIT, but its README identifies LGPL sparse-Cholesky dependencies, an MPL2 sparse-LU alternative selected with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"BUILD_FREE_LICENSE"}),", and separate optional Gurobi terms. Selected build dependencies, not the project badge alone, determine the review scope."]}),`
