`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"validate-geometry-before-relaxing-cooking-safeguards",children:"Validate geometry before relaxing cooking safeguards"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"MeshCollider.cookingOptions"})," controls conversion into physics query/contact support structures. With validity checks disabled, valid inputs are the caller's responsibility and invalid data can produce undefined behavior. This is a separate operation from visual mesh import or format validation. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/MeshCollider-cookingOptions.html",children:"cookingOptions"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Unity requires an alternative validator if cleaning or vertex welding is disabled: cleaning-off meshes must avoid degenerate triangles, including near-zero/infinite-area examples; welding-off meshes must not contain colocated vertices. Read/write access is required for a negatively scaled convex collider, a skewed/sheared transform (including scaled-parent/rotated-child configurations), or nondefault cooking options. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/prepare-mesh-for-mesh-collider.html",children:"Prepare meshes"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The component reference describes four flags: ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"CookForFasterSimulation"})," trades additional preprocessing/storage for runtime work; ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"EnableMeshCleaning"})," attempts to remove degenerates/artifacts; ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"WeldColocatedVertices"})," combines equal-position vertices; ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"UseFastMidphase"})," selects the fastest available platform midphase, with the legacy algorithm available if problems occur. Convex colliders have a documented 255-triangle limit. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Provides Contacts"}),", disabled by default, requests ongoing contact generation even without a usual recipient; lack of contact observations therefore needs configuration context. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/class-MeshCollider.html",children:"MeshCollider reference"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed gate, not an upstream guarantee:"})," record geometry revision/hash, units, winding, vertex/index/triangle counts, finite-coordinate checks, area tolerance and colocated-vertex policy. Keep project tolerances explicit; these pages do not define a universal safe epsilon. A render mesh with duplicated UV/normal-seam vertices may need a distinct collision mesh. Retain enabled flags and rejected-input diagnostics. Do not promise that cleaning repairs arbitrary generated geometry."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"bake-reuse-and-invalidate-deliberately",children:"Bake, reuse and invalidate deliberately"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Physics.BakeMesh(meshID, convex, cookingOptions)"})," returns void; baking runs on the calling thread and stores data on the mesh instance. Player calls need Read/Write enabled, while Editor geometry is available without that setting. Reuse requires identical cooking options, unchanged geometry and a shareable transform: nonnegative, unskewed scaling, or negative scaling for nonconvex colliders. Adding a MeshCollider to an object already carrying a MeshFilter can automatically assign ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"sharedMesh"})," and trigger baking. Thread safety does not permit simultaneous bakes of the same mesh; that case is undefined. The documented Job System example completes work before main-thread collider creation. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/Physics.BakeMesh.html",children:"BakeMesh"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Assigning ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"sharedMesh"})," after changes to vertices, indices or triangles rebuilds collider shapes. This documents assignment-triggered rebuilding; do not infer that a prior bake covers later mesh mutations. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/MeshCollider-sharedMesh.html",children:"sharedMesh"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed gate:"})," keep separate records for input validation, bake return/diagnostics, collider assignment, measured reuse and gameplay acceptance. Deduplicate scheduled mesh IDs and serialize per-mesh cooks; parallelize only distinct meshes. A void return is not a fidelity report. Record target platform, exact engine build, convex choice, flag bitmask and full transform hierarchy. Use diagnostics and profiler evidence to establish actual recooking cost; no portable disk-cache or cross-session reuse contract is established here."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"accept-the-collision-shape",children:"Accept the collision shape"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Concave MeshColliders are supported as static or kinematic geometry, and collide with convex colliders rather than other concave colliders. Convex conversion fills concavities into a hull. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/mesh-colliders-introduction.html",children:"Mesh collider introduction"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Convex geometry has no holes/entrances and must have nonzero volume. Unity may thicken a convex plane/quad by up to 0.05 times its longest in-plane dimension. Thus even a visually correct plane or doorway can acquire materially different collision geometry. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/MeshCollider-convex.html",children:"convex"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed gate:"})," define allowed doorway clearance, ledge height, wall thickness and hull approximation error before choosing convex versus triangle-mesh/compound representation. Treat the documented triangle limit as a collider constraint, not proof that any source mesh below the limit will cook successfully, or that source polygon count equals final hull count. This research establishes no exact rejection/error-code contract for over-limit hulls."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"interpret-queries-separately-from-contacts",children:"Interpret queries separately from contacts"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Physics.ComputePenetration"})," reports whether the supplied poses overlap and, when true, a minimum separation translation for collider A. False leaves direction/distance undefined. At least one collider must be a box, sphere, capsule or convex MeshCollider. Supplying hypothetical position/rotation does not move the scene; this operation does not need spatial structures updated first. It ignores backfaced triangles regardless of ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"queriesHitBackfaces"}),". ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/Physics.ComputePenetration.html",children:"ComputePenetration"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Ordinary physics queries omit back-face hits by default. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/Physics-queriesHitBackfaces.html",children:"queriesHitBackfaces"}),". ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Physics.SyncTransforms"})," manually flushes transform changes, including effects on child colliders, to physics. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/Physics.SyncTransforms.html",children:"SyncTransforms"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed gate:"})," retain query type, collider pair, poses/scales, face direction, layer/trigger policy, transform synchronization and simulation-step context. A front-side ray hit does not demonstrate two-sided contact behavior or traversability. A penetration result is not a simulated contact manifold or whole-scene collision proof. Do not generalize ComputePenetration's synchronization exception to broadphase queries."]}),`
