`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"RationalTime(value, rate)"})," represents value/rate seconds, with double-valued fields. Rescaling changes value as well as rate; copying the value and substituting a new rate changes time. The pinned ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"to_frames()"})," uses an integer cast, so it is not a lossless subframe transport. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"TimeRange"})," uses an inclusive start and exclusive end. Negative durations can be constructed but are invalid for its logical predicates. Keep the value/rate pairs and declare any final engine-frame quantization rather than silently truncating them. A proposed delivery preflight should additionally reject nonfinite values; that is stricter than the inspected NaN/nonpositive-rate validity predicate. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO/blob/44236713c1db295a6ffc66189ae98dbdfd0cb9c4/src/opentime/rationalTime.h#L20-L88",children:"RationalTime implementation"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO/blob/44236713c1db295a6ffc66189ae98dbdfd0cb9c4/src/opentime/rationalTime.h#L226-L233",children:"integer frame conversion"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO/blob/44236713c1db295a6ffc66189ae98dbdfd0cb9c4/src/opentime/timeRange.h#L21-L108",children:"range boundaries/validity"})]}),`
