`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["OTIO permits a source range outside available media. An interior transition overlaps the neighboring edit without extending track length: its parent start is the cut minus ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"in_offset"}),", and duration is ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"in_offset + out_offset"}),". ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"visible_range()"})," adds a preceding transition's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"in_offset"})," as head media and a following transition's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"out_offset"})," as tail media. Thus validating only trimmed ranges misses required handles. The documentation permits unavailable transition media without defining playback fallback; it separately disallows adjacent transitions, overlapping transitions on one clip, and offsets beyond neighboring edit durations. Treat these as explicit preflight checks rather than assuming every parse enforces them. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://opentimelineio.readthedocs.io/en/v0.18.1/tutorials/otio-timeline-structure.html#transitions",children:"Transition and media rules"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO/blob/44236713c1db295a6ffc66189ae98dbdfd0cb9c4/src/opentimelineio/track.cpp#L46-L165",children:"placement and handles"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO/blob/44236713c1db295a6ffc66189ae98dbdfd0cb9c4/src/opentimelineio/item.cpp#L60-L84",children:"visible range calculation"})]}),`
