`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed acceptance contract."})," Add an artifact gate before the localization work order: freeze licensed font and representative corpus → subset with explicit missing-character/layout policy → retain subset diagnostics → run an appropriate Font Bakery profile → sanitize a separate candidate if intended → compare original/derivative hashes → test shaped strings and fallback behavior in the target renderer. Preserve layout-feature choices and exact check profile/version."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Failure/recovery/persistence."})," Successful subsetting with defaults is not coverage evidence. Sanitization can change bytes; retain both artifacts and rerun shaping/coverage against the actual shipped candidate. A passing structural or metadata check does not establish language coverage, acceptable appearance, accessibility or font redistribution rights. Fix source/settings and rebuild; do not suppress failed checks or replace a missing glyph with an unexplained fallback. Atomic output, cancellation and checkpoint-resume semantics remain unverified."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Unimplemented fixture:"})," a requested absent Unicode character, combining sequence, required shaping feature and deliberately malformed font table. Pair structural results with actual rendered-language acceptance; neither replaces the other."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Version/license scope:"})," rolling sources; fontTools README documents Python 3.11+ at review, not an environment probe. Project licenses: fontTools MIT, Font Bakery Apache-2.0, OTS BSD-3-Clause. Font files and optional dependencies have independent terms; Font Bakery is not an official Google-supported product."]}),`
