`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Documented operations and fields."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Shopify/toxiproxy",children:"Toxiproxy"})," is an HTTP/CLI-controlled TCP proxy. Latency toxics default downstream; symmetric delay requires configuring both directions. Its unauthenticated control API must not be exposed to untrusted networks. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man8/tc-netem.8.html",children:"Linux netem's manual"})," documents delay/loss/duplication/corruption and seeded randomness, but timer granularity affects delay/rate fidelity; realistic TCP tests have placement constraints, including receiver ingress guidance."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/pond3r/ggpo",children:"GGPO"})," uses predicted inputs and speculative execution for rollback; its checked README documents Windows builds and the Vector War sample. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL3/SDL_AttachVirtualJoystick",children:"SDL3 virtual joystick attachment"})," is available since 3.2.0, can be called from any thread and returns zero on failure. Virtual devices accept program-provided inputs without physical hardware."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed acceptance contract."})," Extend the multiplayer work order by specifying protocol, direction, placement and measured impairment rather than a single “lag” parameter. Toxiproxy TCP behavior cannot demonstrate impaired UDP. A seed alone does not establish reproducibility across kernel/timer/load differences. For rollback, separately test state save/restore and repeated external side effects. For virtual input, bind device identity and injected schedule to observed game ticks/events; attachment success is not input consumption or physical-device equivalence."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Failure/recovery/persistence."})," Reject unsupported protocol coverage, unobserved impairment, stale device handles and rollback duplication of rewards/audio/network effects. Keep process-owned fixtures isolated; preserve pre-test state and confirm cleanup. Host network changes require explicit authority and a restoration plan; none are performed or authorized by this note. Timeout does not prove the fault was removed. Archive traffic/event/state evidence, not merely configured fault values."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Unimplemented fixture:"})," TCP downstream-only delay contrasted with both directions; rollback after a one-shot effect; virtual-device attach failure and reconnect. No universal cross-platform determinism, literal zero latency, haptics fidelity or durable transaction guarantee is claimed."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Version/license scope:"})," Toxiproxy and GGPO declare MIT; netem package and SDL licensing were not established by the cited function/manual pages. Installed versions and platform support remain unknown. SDL's “since 3.2.0” marker is an API minimum, not a tested package pin."]}),`
