`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Checked ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"2026-10-18"})," against official ozz-animation ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"0.17.0"}),", commit ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"744eb9d99f606eda849acb0b1204f7a3dc20bca1"})," (2026-08-01). Source inspection only; no library installation, build or animation execution. This adds runtime sampling/compression gates to existing retargeting and interchange notes. API documentation, static source findings and proposed GameMap gates are distinguished below. [S1]"]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"compact-operational-chain",children:"Compact operational chain"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"1. Bind clip tracks to the actual rig."})," RawAnimation documents positive duration, strictly ordered keys and key times within the clip. Static validation also caps track count, but does not establish finite transforms or semantic joint identity. The optimizer checks track count against skeleton joint count; equality cannot prove matching joint order, hierarchy or rest pose. Proposed gate: preserve importer mapping, ordered joint names/parents/rest poses, units and basis alongside source hashes. SkeletonBuilder emits depth-first indices; an Animation header comment says breadth-first, so use actual emitted order rather than that inconsistent comment. [S3–S6, S8, S16–S17]"]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"2. Reduce keys into a distinct candidate."})," AnimationOptimizer documents hierarchy-aware key reduction, global settings and per-joint overrides. Defaults are tolerance 0.001 and distance 0.1, annotated 1 mm/10 cm; record asset units. Distance approximates off-joint influence rather than evaluating a skin mesh. Static implementation rejects aliased input/output; for a distinct destination it clears output before validation/count checks. Preserve the source and require a true result before promoting the candidate. A failed call is not a rollback mechanism for a prior destination. [S7–S8]"]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"3. Build runtime compression separately."})," AnimationBuilder does not perform keyframe optimization. Static implementation nevertheless quantizes translation/scale to half floats and compresses quaternion components; therefore optimizer tolerance is not a certificate for final decoded error. Retain original raw, reduced raw and runtime derivative identities. Require a non-null built animation and record iframe settings; iframes support seeking, not fidelity validation. Compare original raw sampling with the final runtime samples under declared positional and angular tolerances. [S9–S10]"]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"4. Sample a complete pose with owned state."})," SamplingJob documents local-space output at a clamped normalized ratio. It can intentionally omit trailing tracks when output is short and leave surplus SoA transforms unchanged. Static Validate accepts a nonempty short output if context capacity suffices. Proposed full-pose gate: require count compatibility and at least ceil(joints/4) SoA transforms; Run()==true alone is insufficient. Keep animation, context and buffers alive through execution; give concurrent evaluations exclusive mutable contexts/outputs. Resize invalidates the context. Explicitly Invalidate before an animation is replaced in reused storage: automatic detection uses its address, and the header warns address reuse can crash. [S11–S12]"]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"5. Convert with the recorded hierarchy."})," LocalToModelJob requires skeleton-ordered local transforms and one output model matrix per joint. Mesh remapping/inverse-bind application remains separate. Its optional root matrix can prefix world placement. Partial updates require already-valid parent model state; stale parents can invalidate an otherwise successful update. Proposed acceptance starts with a full-hierarchy conversion, then separately tests partial updates. Successful conversion establishes neither skin deformation nor root-motion extraction. [S13–S14]"]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"6. Accept motion in the consumer."})," The official optimizer sample compares raw/runtime joint-origin translations after local-to-model. That metric can miss rotated skin surfaces. Proposed unexecuted fixture: an asymmetric rig with a long limb, nonuniform scale, leaf rotation, planted foot and moving root; include a same-count swapped-track negative control, undersized output, backward seeks, loop boundaries and animation replacement. Compare sampled joint positions/orientations and skinned vertices, then separately evaluate foot sliding/penetration, contacts and root trajectory using declared consumer policies. Finite samples do not establish continuous-time bounds. [S15]"]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"recovery-evidence-and-scope",children:"Recovery, evidence and scope"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Retain pins, mappings, settings, sample schedule, native return values and error observations. Correct failed stages from preserved inputs; replace caches and rerun all downstream checks. Cancellation, durable archive writes, crash recovery, cross-version archive compatibility, engine bindings and whole-game determinism remain unverified. No ACL comparison is claimed. ozz-animation's inspected license is MIT; preserve its notices and review dependency/media terms separately. All proposed gates remain unimplemented. [S2]"}),`
