`,e.jsxs(t.table,{children:[e.jsx(t.thead,{children:e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Surface"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Source-inspected contract"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Proposed GameMap gate"})]})}),e.jsxs(t.tbody,{children:[e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Skeleton/output mapping"}),e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Transform-track descriptors carry parent and output indices. Output indices are unique/contiguous; an invalid output index strips a track. Default sub-tracks are omitted from compressed storage. If the chosen defaults are not identity, the decoder must supply those values; the compressed tracks alone cannot reconstruct them. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/nfrechette/acl/blob/3ee568542eca4428e1041908b4a644b98e7885bd/includes/acl/core/track_desc.h",children:"Track descriptor"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Retain parent/output mapping, stripped-track policy and exact default/reference pose alongside compressed bytes. Do not judge compatibility by track count alone."})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Error scale"}),e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["The same descriptor measures error on a rigidly deformed shell around each transform, with default precision ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"0.01 cm"})," and shell distance ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"3 cm"}),"; units must be adjusted when different. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/nfrechette/acl/blob/3ee568542eca4428e1041908b4a644b98e7885bd/includes/acl/core/track_desc.h",children:"Track descriptor"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Preserve units, per-track precision and shell distance. A small compression-error setting is not a universal visible-mesh, foot-contact or gameplay tolerance."})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Host transform arithmetic"}),e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["The default QVV error metric cannot represent shear/skew from composed bone chains. The matrix variant handles scaled object-space composition, but extreme scales/translations can accumulate numerical error. For error measurement, the additive clip is applied to the base clip in local space; object-space additive blending is ignored. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/nfrechette/acl/blob/3ee568542eca4428e1041908b4a644b98e7885bd/docs/error_metrics.md",children:"Metric guidance"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Match the actual host's hierarchy, scale and additive convention before interpreting compression fidelity; separately inspect skinning and contact."})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Sampling and loop policy"}),e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Decoding binds a context, seeks with an explicit rounding policy, and writes through a track writer. Interpolated, floor, ceil, nearest and per-track rounding are distinct. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/nfrechette/acl/blob/3ee568542eca4428e1041908b4a644b98e7885bd/docs/decompressing_a_track_list.md",children:"Decoding guide"})," Wrap playback introduces a synthetic repeat of the first sample and changes duration; full-duration sampling then returns that first sample. This can conflict with absolute root displacement, and wrapping is unsuitable for non-looping clips. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/nfrechette/acl/blob/3ee568542eca4428e1041908b4a644b98e7885bd/docs/handling_looping_playback.md",children:"Looping guide"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Record context/clip identity, times, rounding and looping policy. Compare the loop seam and accumulated root trajectory separately; one pose at “clip end” cannot establish total travel."})]})]})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Fixture template:"})," compare original, optimized and decoded clips on an asymmetric hierarchy with a non-identity reference pose, stripped tracks, nonuniform scale, an additive layer and nonzero root displacement. Check authored sample times and between-key times, the loop seam and repeated cycles. Preserve per-joint/world-space observations and the rendered skin; foot sliding, penetration and controller/root-motion application require actual target-project observations, not a library success result or compression ratio."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"godot-retargeting-normalized-keys-are-not-controller-travel",children:"Godot retargeting: normalized keys are not controller travel"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Checked ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"2026-10-19"})," against official ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Godot 4.4-stable"}),", commit ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41"}),". The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/git/ref/tags/4.4-stable",children:"tag reference"})," and ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/version.py#L1-L9",children:"version file"})," establish this selected source version, not an installed engine or later-release compatibility. Static source review only; no import, retargeting or playback was executed."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Boundary."})," Accept the imported animation together with its target skeleton and root-motion consumer, not just matching clip samples. This extends the preceding compression gates: on the default postprocessing path for a valid skeletal position track, an unchanged animation resource can legitimately produce different positional motion on skeletons with different ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"motion_scale"}),". This does not apply indiscriminately to every animation track. Reuse the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/engine-operation-contracts/#runtime-animation-observation-gates",children:"runtime animation observation gates"})," for playback timing, visible root-transform cancellation and movement ownership; the additional boundary here is imported keys → target-scaled samples → extracted deltas → controller travel."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source-observed contract."})}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/editor/import/3d/post_import_plugin_skeleton_rest_fixer.cpp#L464-L473",children:"rest fixer"})," sets ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"motion_scale"})," from the absolute global-rest Y coordinate of the profile's scale-base bone only when that bone is found and the value is positive. If the scale-base bone is missing or its absolute global-rest Y coordinate is zero, this branch retains the existing scale rather than reporting an explicit failure. Enabling normalization is not evidence that a new scale was calculated; the later normalization pass can still use that retained scale. Its ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/editor/import/3d/post_import_plugin_skeleton_rest_fixer.cpp#L850-L889",children:"normalization pass"})," divides eligible position keys by that scale; compressed tracks are skipped, and the pass is restricted to the relevant skeletons. Missing BoneMap/profile causes an ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/editor/import/3d/post_import_plugin_skeleton_rest_fixer.cpp#L86-L100",children:"earlier return"}),", not a per-clip success verdict."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["The default ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/scene/animation/animation_mixer.cpp#L997-L1025",children:"AnimationMixer postprocessor"})," multiplies skeletal position samples by the ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"receiving"})," skeleton's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"motion_scale"}),"; a script override can replace that default. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/scene/animation/animation_mixer.cpp#L1311-L1356",children:"root-motion calculation"})," also postprocesses position samples before forming deltas. Thus manually multiplying a returned delta by the same scale again would double-apply it on this default path. This is a control-flow inference, not a measured defect."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/doc/classes/AnimationMixer.xml#L106-L174",children:"root-motion API contract"})," distinguishes per-update displacement from the blended position accumulator. A wrong track type returns zero displacement, and differencing accumulator values may jump at loops. A zero delta is therefore not a complete validity or stationary-clip verdict; validate the configured path/type separately. The linked runtime observation gates already cover visible transform cancellation and the consuming controller."]}),`
`]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed acceptance, unimplemented."})," Record source/imported animation identities, BoneMap/profile, normalization and retarget-method settings, source and target rest transforms, measured ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"motion_scale"})," values, resolved root-motion path/type, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"root_motion_local"}),", any key-value override, update time/delta and controller code/configuration. Keep separate outputs for imported key values, evaluated target-bone pose, extracted root-motion deltas and final controller/world trajectory. Controller collision and rotation policies can make actual travel differ from the animation request; preserve both rather than declaring either one the other. If a turning extension is tested, convert each local delta into the consistent controller/world frame required by that rotation policy before accumulating; a raw local-space sum is not world travel."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Unexecuted fixtures."})," Evaluate the same imported moving-root clip on two otherwise identical target skeletons with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"motion_scale"})," values 1 and 2. Use a valid skeletal root-motion path, default postprocessing, one clip at weight 1, no modifiers or rotation, and ordinary non-seek playback over the same interior time interval. Require demonstrably nonzero baseline displacement over that interval, explicit numerical tolerances and observations taken after the mixer update, so a zero/zero result cannot pass vacuously. The proposed oracle is ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"postprocessed_sample₂ = 2 × postprocessed_sample₁"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"extracted_delta₂ = 2 × extracted_delta₁"}),", not a ratio of visible bone poses or blended accumulators. This checks default runtime motion-scale evaluation, not independently successful importer normalization or retarget mapping. Record controller travel separately using the existing runtime observation gates rather than duplicating their playback and movement-owner fixture. Add missing scale-base bone, zero scale-base height and invalid root-motion track type. In a separate loop-seam case, distinguish accumulated per-update deltas from accumulator differences; an accumulator endpoint is not total travel. Require the harness to flag unexpected scale/path configuration; do not assume the engine reports these as failures. These are proposed assertions, not executed results."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Recovery and limits."})," Preserve the original scene, import settings and failed candidate. Fix the explicit map, scale or consumer contract and reimport into an isolated candidate; do not compensate silently by changing clip keys or controller speed. No universal stride/contact guarantee, continuous-time bound, modifier-chain correctness, crash-safe reimport or cross-version result is established. The inspected engine code uses ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/LICENSE.txt",children:"MIT/Expat"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/COPYRIGHT.txt#L1-L46",children:"third-party license inventory"}),", plugins and animation/model rights remain separate."]}),`
