`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["For the first adapter, constrain input to one unscaled sprite, its complete timeline, composited visible layers, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"json-array"}),", packed layout, per-frame trimming, zero inner padding, and no crop, grid/layer/tag/slice splitting, or play-subtags mode. Keep empty frames. Explicitly request tag and slice metadata. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.aseprite.org/docs/cli/",children:"CLI documentation"})," distinguishes PNG output from JSON output, offers hash/array shapes, and makes metadata inclusion and some layer operations option-dependent. The pinned ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/blob/331e898ef405d919539c03fd1675691cfa16c3a3/src/app/cli/app_options.cpp",children:"CLI options"})," distinguish individual-frame ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--trim"})," for sheets from whole-sprite ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--trim-sprite"}),"."]}),`
