`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"preserve-coordinate-systems-and-time-units",children:"Preserve coordinate systems and time units"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/blob/331e898ef405d919539c03fd1675691cfa16c3a3/docs/ase-file-specs.md#slice-chunk-0x2022",children:"Aseprite file specification"})," defines slice pivots relative to the slice origin. For an unscaled frame, derive the source-canvas anchor as ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"slice.bounds.position + slice.pivot"}),"; its trimmed-image coordinate is that anchor minus ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"spriteSourceSize.position"}),". A pivot without its slice origin is insufficient. Specify the active slice key for each frame and an explicit fallback or rejection when no pivot exists."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["A proposed Godot adapter can reconstruct the canvas with an ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"AtlasTexture"}),": ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"region = frame"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"margin.position = spriteSourceSize.position"}),", and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"margin.size = sourceSize - frame.size"}),". This is a derivation for the restricted profile above: the pinned ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/resources/atlas_texture.cpp#L33-L53",children:"AtlasTexture implementation"})," adds margin size to region size, and ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/resources/atlas_texture.cpp#L157-L220",children:"drawing"})," applies margin position. The pinned ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/aseprite/laf/blob/500768cccc6447e3b7816bedbfcb378a5c5222e5/gfx/packing_rects.cpp#L104-L126",children:"packing implementation"})," uses shape padding for placement without enlarging the returned rectangle; the exported frame already excludes extrusion. This reconstruction remains untested here. For an unflipped node with a constant source anchor, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"AnimatedSprite2D.centered = false"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"offset = -anchor"})," is a candidate placement convention; its ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/doc/classes/AnimatedSprite2D.xml#L83-L101",children:"documented properties"})," distinguish centering from drawing offset. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/2d/animated_sprite_2d.cpp#L269-L300",children:"draw implementation"})," confirms this offset path. Changing anchors or flips require additional handling."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Aseprite frame durations are milliseconds in the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/blob/331e898ef405d919539c03fd1675691cfa16c3a3/docs/ase-file-specs.md#frames",children:"frame specification"}),". Godot's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_spriteframes.html#class-spriteframes-method-get-frame-duration",children:"SpriteFrames contract"})," uses relative durations: seconds equal relative duration divided by animation FPS and absolute playing speed. At baseline playing speed 1, convert milliseconds ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"d"})," to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"d × FPS / 1000"}),". Thus 80 ms at 10 FPS becomes 0.8. Copying milliseconds directly is valid only with a matching timebase, such as 1000 FPS at speed 1. Record subsequent playback-speed changes separately."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Godot's loop setting is Boolean. Aseprite's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/blob/331e898ef405d919539c03fd1675691cfa16c3a3/docs/ase-file-specs.md#tags-chunk-0x2018",children:"tag specification"})," also defines finite repetition and direction; zero repeat is unspecified and differs between UI and export playback. Declare how finite repeats, reverse and ping-pong are translated, or reject them. Never infer identical playback from matching tag names."]}),`
