`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Tiled GIDs are map-local. The same tile can acquire another GID when tilesets change order. Interpret the value as unsigned 32-bit, extract flags, and clear all four high bits before lookup: horizontal ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0x80000000"}),", vertical ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0x40000000"}),", diagonal/hex-60 ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0x20000000"}),", hex-120 ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0x10000000"}),". Clear the fourth flag even for non-hexagonal maps. Zero denotes an empty cell; otherwise choose the largest ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"firstgid"})," not exceeding the stripped value, then subtract it. Orthogonal/isometric transforms apply diagonal swapping before horizontal/vertical flips; hexagonal flags have different semantics. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://doc.mapeditor.org/en/stable/reference/global-tile-ids/",children:"GID contract"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mapeditor/tiled/blob/1fd984638f9898af920103799bcd68b467287295/docs/reference/global-tile-ids.rst",children:"pinned documentation"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["A valid range is insufficient: image-collection tilesets can have gaps, including local IDs above ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"tilecount"}),". External TSX files omit map-specific ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"firstgid"}),". Verify actual tile existence and preserve tileset identity plus local ID as the transfer key. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://doc.mapeditor.org/en/stable/reference/tmx-map-format/#tileset",children:"TMX tilesets"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Godot atlas transformations instead use alternative-ID flags ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"4096"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"8192"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"16384"}),"; raw Tiled GIDs cannot be copied into them. The adapter needs an explicit lookup to source ID, atlas coordinates, alternative ID and normalized transform. Validate all eight orthogonal flip combinations against asymmetric artwork rather than assuming names alone establish equivalence. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_tilesetatlassource.html#constants",children:"Godot atlas flags"}),"."]}),`
