`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Infinite-map chunks have independent tile-coordinate origins and dimensions; Tiled's official JSON example includes ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"y: -16"}),". Proposed output coordinates are chunk origin plus within-chunk position, retaining negative values and sparse gaps. Validate decoded element counts per chunk, not against a finite map rectangle; establish an explicit policy for overlapping chunks. Pixel layer offsets remain a separate transform. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://doc.mapeditor.org/en/stable/reference/json-map-format/#chunk",children:"JSON layer/chunk contract"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Godot TileMapLayer serializes coordinates within ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"−32768…32767"}),", wrapping values outside that range. The pinned writer explicitly casts each coordinate to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"int16_t"}),". A populated in-memory layer therefore does not establish a faithful saved map. Reject out-of-range imports or specify a reversible partition/rebasing scheme before saving; compare logical coordinates after fresh reopen. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_tilemaplayer.html#description",children:"4.5 persistence warning"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/2d/tile_map_layer.cpp#L3196-L3233",children:"writer, lines 3196–3233"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"3-carry-geometry-independently-of-tile-images",children:"3. Carry geometry independently of tile images"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Tiled distinguishes grid size, image size, drawing offset and tile-object alignment. Larger layer tiles extend above/right of their bottom-left anchor. Unspecified tile-object alignment defaults to bottom-left for orthogonal maps; explicit ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"objectalignment"})," can override it. Polygon points are relative to their object, and object rotation is clockwise around its position. Margin/spacing, tile offset and layer offset are separate inputs. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://doc.mapeditor.org/en/stable/reference/tmx-map-format/",children:"TMX geometry definitions"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The pinned renderer scales tile offsets with rendered dimensions and compensates for rectangular-image dimension swapping during diagonal transforms. Its collision-overlay path composes each object's own rotation with the tile fragment's translation, rotation and scale. This is evidence for authored geometry placement, ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"not"})," a physics-engine importer. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mapeditor/tiled/blob/1fd984638f9898af920103799bcd68b467287295/src/libtiled/maprenderer.cpp#L468-L523",children:"Cell rendering, lines 468–523"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mapeditor/tiled/blob/1fd984638f9898af920103799bcd68b467287295/src/libtiled/maprenderer.cpp#L631-L655",children:"collision overlay, lines 631–655"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Godot's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"map_to_local()"})," gives a cell center and ignores the per-tile ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"texture_origin"})," drawing offset. Do not use that center as an image-anchor oracle. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_tilemaplayer.html#class-tilemaplayer-method-map-to-local",children:"Coordinate conversion"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_tiledata.html#class-tiledata-property-texture-origin",children:"texture origin"}),"."]}),`
