`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Godot's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"set_cell"})," accepts the three-part tile identity; setting source/alternative to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"-1"})," or atlas coordinates to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(-1,-1)"})," erases the cell. Updates are batched at frame end and queued only inside the scene tree; scene tiles initialize after their parent. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"update_internals()"})," performs internal processing immediately; this is not an independently observed rendering/physics completion fence. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/2d/tile_map_layer.cpp#L3062-L3064",children:"Implementation, lines 3062–3064"}),". ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"notify_runtime_tile_data_update()"})," also defers work, and runtime callback subresources may be shared with the TileSet, requiring duplication before mutation. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_tilemaplayer.html",children:"TileMapLayer 4.5 API"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["A sharper readback boundary appears in source: ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"_build_runtime_update_tile_data_for_cell"})," makes the runtime duplicate, whereas ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"get_cell_tile_data()"})," retrieves the atlas source's base data. Thus that getter alone cannot attest to the applied runtime override. Record callback inputs/results and observe the affected subsystem independently. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/2d/tile_map_layer.cpp#L1693-L1738",children:"Runtime copy, lines 1693–1738"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/2d/tile_map_layer.cpp#L2820-L2832",children:"getter, lines 2820–2832"}),"."]}),`
